        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Home Depot sells treadmills, but only online and only from
            budget brands with short warranties.</strong> If what you want is a basic walking pad and
            you have checked the specification table, the brand and the 90-day return terms, it can
            do the job. For anything more, it is the wrong shop.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy the treadmill from a retailer that carries established brands, compare the delivered
            price with
            <a href="/treadmills-for-sale/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">other places to buy</a>,
            and use Home Depot for what it is good at: the mat, the flooring and the room the
            machine will stand in.
          </p>
